{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_28","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba 'protocol/core.md' | sed -n '150,330p'\"","aggregated_output":"   150\t   `conflicting_skill_manifests` and MUST NOT install either value.\n   151\t4. The existence of an invalid modern manifest is an error and MUST NOT fall\n   152\t   back to the other filename or to `agents/runtime.json`.\n   153\t\n   154\t| Schema | Added behavior |\n   155\t|---|---|\n   156\t| 1 | exported script and system commands |\n   157\t| 2 | `runtime_roots`, command dependencies, strict top-level fields |\n   158\t| 3 | REQUIRED capability declaration |\n   159\t| 4 | transitive skill requirements |\n   160\t| 5 | MCP server requirements |\n   161\t| 6 | declarative compiled commands and context-excluded `build_roots` |\n   162\t\n   163\tVersion gates are downward: a field introduced by a later version MUST be\n   164\trejected in an earlier one. Schema 1 preserves its deployed extension behavior;\n   165\tschemas 2 through 6 reject unknown fields. In particular, schema 1 through 5\n   166\tMUST reject `build_roots`, a command with `type: \"build\"`, and every build-only\n   167\tfield. Their script, system, runtime-root, capability, dependency, context,\n   168\thash, and marker-v1 behavior is unchanged.\n   169\t\n   170\t### 4.1 Runtime roots and commands\n   171\t\n   172\tEvery runtime root and script command path MUST be a portable relative path\n   173\tthat exists in the snapshot. Runtime roots MUST name directories, be unique,\n   174\tand be pairwise disjoint. For schema 2 and later, every script command path\n   175\tMUST fall within one declared runtime root when any roots are declared.\n   176\t\n   177\tA script command declares at least one of `unix_path` and `win_path`. A system\n   178\tcommand declares a non-empty bare executable name and MAY include a hint. A\n   179\tmissing system command fails installation with the hint. The command name is\n   180\tthe shim name and one active name has exactly one owner.\n   181\t\n   182\t### 4.2 Build roots and the closed `go-v1` command\n   183\t\n   184\t`build_roots` and build commands exist only in manifest schema 6. Every build\n   185\troot MUST be a portable relative path other than `.`, MUST name a real,\n   186\tlink-free directory in the immutable raw snapshot, and MUST be unique and\n   187\tpairwise disjoint. No build root may equal, contain, or be contained by a\n   188\truntime root. Every declared build root MUST be referenced by at least one\n   189\tbuild command.\n   190\t\n   191\tA build command has exactly this package-controlled surface:\n   192\t\n   193\t```json\n   194\t{\"type\":\"build\",\"driver\":\"go-v1\",\"source_dir\":\"build/cmd/tool\"}\n   195\t```\n   196\t\n   197\tThe object MUST contain exactly `type`, `driver`, and `source_dir`; the driver\n   198\tMUST be the closed identifier `go-v1`. `source_dir` MUST be a real, link-free\n   199\tdirectory below exactly one declared build root and MAY equal that root, but\n   200\tMUST NOT be `.`. The containing build root is the command's `build_root`; it\n   201\tMUST contain `go.mod` directly, and that file MUST be the nearest ancestor\n   202\t`go.mod` of `source_dir`. An intervening module is invalid.\n   203\t\n   204\tThe manager MUST derive the artifact-relative path solely from the command\n   205\tname: `bin/<command>` on Unix and `bin/<command>.exe` on Windows. A package\n   206\tMUST NOT select a program, arguments, environment, tags, flags, toolchain,\n   207\toutput path, build script, hook, plugin, generator, or post-build action.\n   208\tUnsupported drivers MUST fail without falling back to a system command or\n   209\tgeneric build facility. Build commands participate in existing activation,\n   210\tdependency-command selection, portable-name collision, shim collision, and\n   211\tprovider-first closure rules exactly like script commands. Within one closure\n   212\tnode, active build command names MUST be processed in Unicode-scalar lexical\n   213\torder.\n   214\t\n   215\t`go-v1` builds exactly one native executable from exactly one package named\n   216\t`main`. The toolchain MUST be Go 1.23 or newer, operator-trusted rather than\n   217\tpackage-selected, and from a release family tested by the manager against the\n   218\t`go-v1` conformance vectors. The module is the declared build root, dependency\n   219\tresolution is vendor-only and networkless, and workspaces, toolchain switching,\n   220\tcross-compilation, PGO, cgo, package-controlled assembly, host objects,\n   221\tgenerators, tests, plugins, overlays, external linking, and libgcc fallback are\n   222\tforbidden.\n   223\t\n   224\tThe manager MUST invoke the resolved `<GOROOT>/bin/go` directly, never through\n   225\ta shell or joined command string. Once per operation it MUST use exactly these\n   226\tpackage-independent argument vectors from a manager-owned empty directory as\n   227\tthe working directory. The bootstrap environment MUST start empty except for\n   228\tindispensable operating-system process variables; use operation-private user,\n   229\tconfiguration, cache, and temporary roots; set `GOENV=off` and\n   230\t`GOTOOLCHAIN=local`, `LC_ALL=C`, and `LANG=C`; and contain no inherited `GOROOT`\n   231\tor target:\n   232\t\n   233\t```text\n   234\tgo telemetry off\n   235\tgo version\n   236\tgo env -json GOROOT GOHOSTOS GOHOSTARCH GOOS GOARCH GO386 GOAMD64 GOARM GOARM64 GOMIPS GOMIPS64 GOPPC64 GORISCV64 GOWASM GOTELEMETRY GOTELEMETRYDIR\n   237\t```\n   238\t\n   239\tFor every active build command, with canonical `source_dir` as the working\n   240\tdirectory, it MUST then use exactly:\n   241\t\n   242\t```text\n   243\tgo list -mod=vendor -deps -json -buildvcs=false -compiler=gc -pgo=off .\n   244\tgo build -mod=vendor -trimpath -buildvcs=false -buildmode=exe -compiler=gc -pgo=off -ldflags=-linkmode=internal -libgcc=none -o <manager-staging-artifact> .\n   245\t```\n   246\t\n   247\tEach line above denotes an argument vector; the `-ldflags=...` value is one\n   248\targument and the output is the manager-derived staging path. During bootstrap\n   249\tand command builds, the environment MUST set `GOPATH`, `GOMODCACHE`, `GOCACHE`,\n   250\t`GOTMPDIR`, `HOME`, `XDG_CONFIG_HOME`, `PATH`, and `TMPDIR` below\n   251\toperation-private roots, with `PATH` naming a manager-owned empty directory. On\n   252\tWindows, `APPDATA`, `LOCALAPPDATA`, `USERPROFILE`, `TEMP`, and `TMP` MUST also\n   253\tbe private.\n   254\t\n   255\tAfter the bootstrap probes, the environment MUST retain the bootstrap settings\n   256\tand add the resolved `GOROOT`, native `GOOS`/`GOARCH`, exactly one applicable\n   257\ttrusted tuning variable, and `GO111MODULE=on`, `GOFLAGS=` (empty), `GOPROXY=off`,\n   258\t`GOSUMDB=off`, `GOPRIVATE=` (empty), `GONOPROXY=none`, `GONOSUMDB=none`,\n   259\t`GOVCS=*:off`, `GOWORK=off`, `CGO_ENABLED=0`, `GO_EXTLINK_ENABLED=0`,\n   260\tand `GOEXPERIMENT=` (empty). It MUST verify `GOTELEMETRY == \"off\"` and that\n   261\t`GOTELEMETRYDIR` is below the operation-private platform configuration root.\n   262\tPackage or ambient Go, compiler, linker, and executable-search variables MUST\n   263\tNOT be inherited.\n   264\t\n   265\tThe complete `go list` stream MUST contain exactly one non-`DepOnly` root with\n   266\t`Name == \"main\"`, no incomplete result, and no `Error` or `DepsErrors`. Only a\n   267\tresult with both `Standard == true` and `Goroot == true` is a trusted toolchain\n   268\tpackage; its directory and every listed input MUST stay below the fingerprinted\n   269\t`GOROOT`. Every other result and its package directory, module file, active Go\n   270\tfile, and embedded input MUST stay below the command's build root. Every result\n   271\tMUST have empty `SysoFiles`; every result with `Standard == false` MUST also\n   272\thave empty `CgoFiles`, `CFiles`, `CXXFiles`, `MFiles`, `HFiles`, `FFiles`,\n   273\t`SFiles`, `SwigFiles`, and `SwigCXXFiles`. Every active non-standard `GoFiles`\n   274\tfile MUST be a regular file below the build root and MUST NOT contain the exact\n   275\tASCII bytes\n   276\t`//go:cgo_import_dynamic`. Any failure occurs before `go build`.\n   277\t\n   278\tOnly the fingerprinted `go` executable and its regular executable children\n   279\tbelow fingerprinted `GOROOT/pkg/tool/<GOHOSTOS>_<GOHOSTARCH>/` may start. The\n   280\tsource snapshot MUST be read-only to child processes and unchanged until the\n   281\tlast child exits. The one output MUST be a bounded regular file inside manager\n   282\tstaging. The manager MUST hash it, set manager-defined executable permissions,\n   283\tand MUST NOT execute it for validation, version discovery, smoke testing,\n   284\tpost-processing, receipt generation, rollback, or any other reason.\n   285\t\n   286\t### 4.3 Capabilities\n   287\t\n   288\tSchema 3 and later require `capabilities`. Capabilities are an audit surface,\n   289\tnot a runtime sandbox:\n   290\t\n   291\t- `network`: `\"none\"` or unique host globs without whitespace or path syntax;\n   292\t- `filesystem`: `\"repo\"`, `\"home-config\"`, or unique portable paths;\n   293\t- `exec`: `\"none\"` or unique bare executable names;\n   294\t- `secrets`: `\"none\"` or unique non-empty secret identifiers;\n   295\t- `env_read`: unique environment-variable names;\n   296\t- `prompt_scope`: an OPTIONAL non-empty purpose statement.\n   297\t\n   298\tMissing OPTIONAL capability fields take their schema defaults.\n   299\t\n   300\t### 4.4 Dependencies\n   301\t\n   302\t`dependencies.commands` contains system requirements. Its legacy `type:\n   303\t\"skill\"` form remains readable, does not create a shim, and produces a\n   304\tmigration warning.\n   305\t\n   306\tEach `dependencies.skills` entry contains `git`, exact `ref`, activation\n   307\t`mode`, and OPTIONAL command narrowing. `ref.kind` is `tag` or `revision`;\n   308\tbranch and range syntax is forbidden. `mode` is `full` (default), `runtime`, or\n   309\t`context`. `commands` is valid only in runtime mode, is non-empty when present,\n   310\tand names exported script or build commands of the provider. Build commands are\n   311\tavailable only from schema 6 providers; schemas 1 through 5 retain script-only\n   312\tcommand narrowing. Duplicates are rejected.\n   313\t\n   314\tEach `dependencies.mcp_servers` entry requires a non-empty `hint`, MAY document\n   315\t`transport` as `stdio` or `http`, and uses `required_in` `any` (default) or\n   316\t`all`.\n   317\t\n   318\tIf neither modern manifest filename exists, `agents/runtime.json` MAY be read\n   319\tas the legacy object `{ \"commands\": { <name>: <portable-relative-path> } }`.\n   320\tWriters MUST NOT create this legacy form.\n   321\t\n   322\t## 5. Project manifests\n   323\t\n   324\t`Skillfile.json` conforms to `skillfile-v1.schema.json`. It contains unique\n   325\tskill declarations and exactly one of `tag`, `branch`, or `revision` for each\n   326\tskill. `source` is a portable relative path below the manager's configured\n   327\tsource root. `git` is used when the source repository is absent. Branches are\n   328\tpermitted only for direct project declarations and development substitutions.\n   329\t\n   330\t`project.alias`, when present, is a non-empty, case-sensitive Unicode label of\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
