{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_29","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba 'profiles/manager.md' | sed -n '80,245p'\"","aggregated_output":"    80\t   snapshot checks, validate every skill package, reject command, shim,\n    81\t   portable-path, case-folding, and platform-path collisions, and verify system,\n    82\t   legacy command, and MCP requirements;\n    83\t8. run source-audit policy, resolve trusted registries and attestations, reject\n    84\t   revocation or strict unknown results, and apply moved-tag policy; and\n    85\t9. only after all preceding gates pass, resolve and fingerprint a trusted\n    86\t   toolchain, derive build inputs and logical cache keys, validate the protected\n    87\t   cache boundary, and inspect eligible receipts and artifacts read-only.\n    88\t\n    89\tSnapshot validation MUST reject links, special files, invalid protocol paths,\n    90\tduplicate encoded paths, and platform path collisions. A build root MUST be a\n    91\treal link-free directory below the snapshot, MUST NOT be `.`, MUST be disjoint\n    92\tfrom every runtime root, and MUST contain the nearest ancestor `go.mod` of each\n    93\tof its commands' `source_dir` values. Every declared build root MUST be used.\n    94\tGenerated artifacts remain only in manager-owned staging and immutable cache\n    95\tstate and MUST NOT become agent-facing context.\n    96\t\n    97\tAudit and registry gates therefore precede both persistent cache lookup and\n    98\tcompilation. Neither a cache hit nor a dry run may bypass source validation,\n    99\tstatic context exclusion, build-source hashing, closure construction, collision\n   100\tchecks, audit, attestation, revocation, or moved-tag evaluation.\n   101\t\n   102\t### 2.2 Closed `go-v1` toolchain and process graph\n   103\t\n   104\tA conforming manager MUST support an operator-trusted Go 1.23 release family\n   105\tthat it has tested against the `go-v1` conformance vectors. It MAY allowlist\n   106\tadditional Go release families only after testing those families against the\n   107\tsame vectors. It MUST reject a pre-1.23, malformed, package-selected, or\n   108\totherwise unknown release, including a newer release merely ordered after a\n   109\tknown one. The launcher is selected independently of the package and MUST be\n   110\tthe regular executable `<GOROOT>/bin/go` (`bin/go.exe` on Windows), never a\n   111\twrapper, repository file, runtime command, project shim, manifest value, or\n   112\texecutable found through the user `PATH`.\n   113\t\n   114\tBefore entering a package-controlled directory, the manager creates an\n   115\toperation-private probe root. From a manager-owned empty working directory it\n   116\tinvokes the resolved `go` executable directly with exactly these first three\n   117\targument vectors, once per operation:\n   118\t\n   119\t```text\n   120\t[<resolved-go>, \"telemetry\", \"off\"]\n   121\t[<resolved-go>, \"version\"]\n   122\t[<resolved-go>, \"env\", \"-json\", \"GOROOT\", \"GOHOSTOS\", \"GOHOSTARCH\", \"GOOS\", \"GOARCH\", \"GO386\", \"GOAMD64\", \"GOARM\", \"GOARM64\", \"GOMIPS\", \"GOMIPS64\", \"GOPPC64\", \"GORISCV64\", \"GOWASM\", \"GOTELEMETRY\", \"GOTELEMETRYDIR\"]\n   123\t```\n   124\t\n   125\tThe manager requires the probed `GOROOT` to equal the independently resolved\n   126\troot, normalizes the bounded single-line `go version` output, verifies the\n   127\tnative host and target values, and only then fingerprints the selected tree\n   128\tusing `curator-go-toolchain-v1` as defined by Protocol Core section 8.2.\n   129\t\n   130\tFor each active build command, in provider-first closure order and then\n   131\tUnicode-scalar lexical command order within a node, it invokes exactly these\n   132\ttwo further argument vectors from the command's canonical `source_dir`:\n   133\t\n   134\t```text\n   135\t[<resolved-go>, \"list\", \"-mod=vendor\", \"-deps\", \"-json\", \"-buildvcs=false\", \"-compiler=gc\", \"-pgo=off\", \".\"]\n   136\t[<resolved-go>, \"build\", \"-mod=vendor\", \"-trimpath\", \"-buildvcs=false\", \"-buildmode=exe\", \"-compiler=gc\", \"-pgo=off\", \"-ldflags=-linkmode=internal -libgcc=none\", \"-o\", <manager-staging-artifact>, \".\"]\n   137\t```\n   138\t\n   139\tThese are the only five Go argument-vector forms. The `-ldflags=...` value and\n   140\tmanager-derived staging path are each one argument. The manager MUST NOT use a\n   141\tshell, command string, response file, package pattern, package-selected\n   142\texecutable, environment value, argument, tag, flag, output path, build recipe,\n   143\thook, plugin, generator, overlay, post-build action, or fallback command.\n   144\t\n   145\tThe bootstrap environment starts empty except for indispensable operating\n   146\tsystem process variables. It sets `GOENV=off`, `GOTOOLCHAIN=local`, `LC_ALL=C`,\n   147\tand `LANG=C`, contains no inherited `GOROOT` or target, and sets `GOPATH`,\n   148\t`GOMODCACHE`, `GOCACHE`, `GOTMPDIR`, `HOME`, `XDG_CONFIG_HOME`, `PATH`, and\n   149\t`TMPDIR` below operation-private roots. `PATH` names a manager-owned empty\n   150\tdirectory. On Windows, `APPDATA`, `LOCALAPPDATA`, `USERPROFILE`, `TEMP`, and\n   151\t`TMP` are also private. The manager MUST verify that `GOTELEMETRY` is `off` and\n   152\tthat `GOTELEMETRYDIR` is below the private platform configuration root.\n   153\t\n   154\tAfter the probes, the build environment retains those settings and adds only\n   155\tthe resolved `GOROOT`, native `GOOS` and `GOARCH`, exactly one applicable\n   156\ttrusted architecture-tuning variable returned by the fixed probe, and:\n   157\t\n   158\t```text\n   159\tGO111MODULE=on\n   160\tGOFLAGS=\n   161\tGOPROXY=off\n   162\tGOSUMDB=off\n   163\tGOPRIVATE=\n   164\tGONOPROXY=none\n   165\tGONOSUMDB=none\n   166\tGOVCS=*:off\n   167\tGOWORK=off\n   168\tCGO_ENABLED=0\n   169\tGO_EXTLINK_ENABLED=0\n   170\tGOEXPERIMENT=\n   171\t```\n   172\t\n   173\tNo ambient or package Go, compiler, assembler, linker, telemetry,\n   174\texecutable-search, workspace, proxy, authentication, or tuning variable may be\n   175\tinherited. `GOOS` and `GOARCH` MUST equal the probed host target; cross-builds\n   176\tare unsupported. Module resolution is vendor-only and networkless. The manager\n   177\tMUST NOT download, tidy, vendor, generate, test, run, install, or fetch a\n   178\tpackage, use a workspace or PGO profile, or switch toolchains. A `go.mod`\n   179\tversion or `toolchain` directive that would require switching to an untrusted or\n   180\tunallowlisted toolchain is rejected rather than downloaded or approximated.\n   181\t\n   182\tOnly the fingerprinted `go` executable and regular executable children below\n   183\tthe fingerprinted `GOROOT/pkg/tool/<GOHOSTOS>_<GOHOSTARCH>/` may start. The\n   184\tsource snapshot is read-only to every child and the toolchain and snapshot MUST\n   185\tremain unchanged until the last child exits. No shell, VCS client, network\n   186\thelper, external compiler, assembler, linker, libgcc helper, or other process\n   187\tmay enter the graph.\n   188\t\n   189\t### 2.3 Dependency and artifact preflight\n   190\t\n   191\tOn a real cache miss, the fixed `go list` command MUST complete before the\n   192\tcorresponding `go build`. Its complete JSON stream MUST cover the root and every\n   193\tactive dependency, contain exactly one non-`DepOnly` root named `main`, contain\n   194\tno incomplete result, `Error`, or `DepsErrors`, and select no tests.\n   195\t\n   196\tOnly a result with both `Standard == true` and `Goroot == true` is a trusted\n   197\ttoolchain package. Its directory and every listed source, module, and embedded\n   198\tinput MUST remain below the fingerprinted `GOROOT`. Every other result, its\n   199\tpackage directory, module file, active Go file, and every active embedded input\n   200\tMUST be a regular file below the command's build root. Escaped, missing,\n   201\tlinked, special, or out-of-root input is rejected.\n   202\t\n   203\tEvery result MUST have empty `SysoFiles`. Every non-standard result MUST also\n   204\thave empty `CgoFiles`, `CFiles`, `CXXFiles`, `MFiles`, `HFiles`, `FFiles`,\n   205\t`SFiles`, `SwigFiles`, and `SwigCXXFiles`. Thus cgo, package-controlled C, C++,\n   206\tObjective-C, Fortran, assembly, SWIG, and host objects are rejected throughout\n   207\tthe active dependency graph. Each active non-standard `GoFiles` file is scanned\n   208\tas exact bytes and rejected if it contains `//go:cgo_import_dynamic`. Any\n   209\tviolation fails before `go build`.\n   210\t\n   211\tThe fixed build forces the native gc compiler, disabled PGO and cgo, and\n   212\tinternal linking with no libgcc. If internal linking cannot produce the output,\n   213\tthe command fails; there is no external-link or libgcc fallback. The only\n   214\toutput is the manager-derived `bin/<command>` or `bin/<command>.exe` at a\n   215\tbounded regular file in operation staging. The manager hashes it and applies\n   216\tmanager-defined executable permissions but MUST NOT execute it for validation,\n   217\tversion discovery, smoke testing, post-processing, receipt generation,\n   218\trollback, repair, or recovery.\n   219\t\n   220\t### 2.4 Build cache and dry-run planning\n   221\t\n   222\tFor each active build command, the manager derives the complete build input,\n   223\tlogical cache key, canonical receipt, receipt hash, and artifact-relative path\n   224\texactly as specified by Protocol Core section 9. Persistent reuse is permitted\n   225\tonly below an implementation-specific cache boundary resolved independently of\n   226\tpackage input and proven manager-created, manager-owned, privately mutable,\n   227\tcontained, regular-file-only, and link-safe. The manager verifies that boundary\n   228\tand every entry component on each lookup and again under the manager-home\n   229\tmutation lock. A manager unable to prove the boundary MUST disable persistent\n   230\treuse.\n   231\t\n   232\tA candidate hit is accepted only after the manager recomputes build-source\n   233\tidentity, cache key, complete expected input, exact canonical receipt bytes and\n   234\thash, manager-derived artifact path, artifact hash, and byte length without\n   235\tfollowing links or executing the artifact. Unknown fields or unsupported\n   236\treceipt, driver, build-source, or toolchain versions are rejected. Internally\n   237\tconsistent bytes outside the protected boundary are not provenance: a real\n   238\toperation rebuilds from the revalidated snapshot into new protected state,\n   239\tdry-run reports `would-rebuild-untrusted-cache`, and status is non-current.\n   240\t\n   241\tA dry run performs all read-only planning and package-independent toolchain\n   242\tprobes above, rechecks generation digests for every shared target it consulted,\n   243\tand removes all operation-private state before returning. It reports, per build\n   244\tcommand, `cache-hit`, `would-preflight-and-build`,\n   245\t`would-rebuild-untrusted-cache`, `corrupt`, or `unsupported`. A cache miss is\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
