r--developer--codex-.log:6904:.task-board/.resources/TASK-260720-poa3ze/TASK-260720-poa3ze_compile-only-build-drivers.md:535:1. Fully validate the raw snapshot before hashing. Do not follow links. Every descendant must be a directory or regular file; reject symbolic links, special files, invalid/non-portable protocol paths, duplicate encoded paths, and platform path collisions.\n.task-board/.resources/TASK-260720-3ag6pi/TASK-260720-3ag6pi_spawn-log_-implementer--developer--codex-.log:6908:.task-board/.resources/TASK-260720-poa3ze/TASK-260720-poa3ze_compile-only-build-drivers.md:685:3. Reject symbolic links, reparse-point escapes, special files, and multiply linked receipt/artifact files. Resolve children relative to a held root/directory handle with no-follow semantics and re-check the opened object; Go's rooted file API is one implementation aid because it rejects names that resolve outside the root ([Go `os.OpenInRoot`](https://pkg.go.dev/os#OpenInRoot)), while Windows DACLs provide the platform access-control boundary ([Microsoft access control](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/win32/secauthz/access-control)).\n.task-board/.resources/TASK-260720-3ag6pi/TASK-260720-3ag6pi_spawn-log_-implementer--developer--codex-.log:6939:.task-board/.resources/TASK-260720-poa3ze/TASK-260720-poa3ze_spawn-log_-reviewer--reviewer--codex-.log:4859:Require `GOTELEMETRY == \"off\"`, require `GOTELEMETRYDIR` below the operation-private root at the platform’s expected `os.UserConfigDir()` location, validate `GOROOT` and the minimum/allowlisted release family, freeze the native target/tuning tuple, and then add explicit `GOROOT`, target, and tuning entries to the environment.\n.task-board/.resources/TASK-260720-3ag6pi/TASK-260720-3ag6pi_spawn-log_-implementer--developer--codex-.log:6944:.task-board/.resources/TASK-260720-poa3ze/TASK-260720-poa3ze_spawn-log_-reviewer--reviewer--codex-.log:4960:1. Fully validate the raw snapshot before hashing. Do not follow links. Every descendant