lease metadata, refs, pins, or provenance. Persist the packet as a task outcome resource and leave the task blocked if human authorization remains necessary.\\nspawn agent resolution: Agent selection: codex via explicit_override\\nspawn launch composition: degraded_contract_unavailable; contract=agents-infra.child-launch-composition; provider=codex; schema=1; diagnostic=composition_contract_unavailable; bare child launch retained\\nspawn queued: [analyst] solution-architect (codex) (run=RUN-260727-791dca, max_parallel=20)\\nspawn run started: [analyst] solution-architect (codex) (run=RUN-260727-791dca)\\n2026-07-27 solution-architecture finding: the direct Go os/exec graph cannot install the required native filesystem/network/process/resource controls before compiler execution. Of the two documented contracts, recommend one identity-verified manager-owned worker plus a fail-closed capability-gated hardened Linux profile; current macOS and Windows profiles must reject before worker/Go. Retain go-v1 before unreleased rc.4 only with an explicit manager-worker-v1 cache/receipt policy revision. Justified gap self-check covered protocol/core §4.2, profiles/manager §§2.2–2.4, SECURITY compile-only/compiler-input, decision 0004, closed policy schema, accepted contract research, and rejected/out-of-scope alternatives: the fixed worker is not package-selected, but the graph change requires human authorization. No new board tasks were created because existing spec, Curator, csk, and downstream owners are the smallest traceable decomposition and implementation must not be presumed before authorization. Exact decision and task/CI map are attached in TASK-260720-1zntv0_host-execution-decision.md.\",\"review\":\"required\",\"status\":\"analysis\",\"task_class\":\"code\"}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
